[English - reference translation]
====================================================================

yunatype ("the Licensor") provides the font management software "Yunatype" to the user under the following terms. By downloading, installing or using the Software, the user agrees to this agreement. If you do not agree, do not install or use the Software.

Article 1 (Definitions)
1. "The Software" means everything distributed by the Licensor, including the Yunatype executable, the installer, the bundled extension for Adobe applications and plugin for Figma, icons and documents.
2. "The User" means any individual, company or other organization that downloads, installs or uses the Software.

Article 2 (Grant of License)
1. The Licensor grants the User a non-exclusive, non-transferable right to use the Software free of charge.
2. The User may use the Software whether as an individual, a company or another organization, and including for business or commercial work.
3. There is no limit on the number of devices. An organization may install and use the Software on its own devices.

Article 3 (Prohibited Acts)
The User must not:
1. Without the Licensor's prior permission, redistribute, repost, sell, lend the Software to unspecified or many people, or bundle it with other software or services. However, sharing the Software unmodified and free of charge with members inside the same organization (company, group, school, etc.) does not require permission. If permission is needed, contact the address in Article 13.
2. Modify the Software, or reverse engineer, decompile or disassemble it, except where such a prohibition is not allowed by law.
3. Remove or alter the copyright and license notices shown in the Software.
4. Use the name and logo "Yunatype" as the name of the User's own product or service.

Article 4 (Ownership and Third-Party Software)
1. Rights in the Software belong to the Licensor or its licensors, except for the rights granted in this agreement.
2. The Software includes software provided by third parties (including open source software), each of which is subject to its own license. Their copyright notices and the full license texts are in "THIRD_PARTY_LICENSES.txt" included with the Software.

Article 5 (The User's Fonts)
1. The Software lists font files that the User specifies and temporarily activates them (registers them with the OS). Rights in fonts belong to their respective owners.
2. The User is responsible for complying with the license of each font. The Licensor is not responsible for how the User uses fonts.
3. The Software does not send the User's font files to any external party.

Article 6 (Privacy)
1. The Software does not collect or transmit the User's information. Settings and data are stored only on the User's device (%LOCALAPPDATA%\Yunatype). Communication with the extension for Adobe applications and the plugin for Figma takes place only within the User's device.
2. However, to check for updates, the Software asks GitHub for the latest version at startup. In doing so, the User's IP address is visible to GitHub. This check can be disabled in Preferences.

Article 7 (Trademarks)
Adobe, Photoshop, Illustrator and InDesign are trademarks or registered trademarks of Adobe Inc.; Figma is a trademark of Figma, Inc.; Windows is a trademark or registered trademark of Microsoft Corporation. The Software is not affiliated with, or endorsed by, these companies.

Article 8 (Disclaimer of Warranty)
The Software is provided "AS IS". The Licensor does not warrant that the Software is free of defects, fit for a particular purpose, or will work without problems with other software or environments.

Article 9 (Limitation of Liability)
1. The Software is provided free of charge. The Licensor is not liable for any damage arising from the use of, or inability to use, the Software (including loss of data, settings or fonts, malfunction of other software, and lost profits), except in cases of the Licensor's intent or gross negligence.
2. Where the above exclusion is not permitted by law, the Licensor's liability is limited to ordinary and direct damage actually incurred by the User.

Article 10 (Termination)
If the User violates this agreement, the license under this agreement terminates automatically. In that case the User must stop using the Software and delete it. Articles 4 to 9 and 11 to 13 survive termination.

Article 11 (Changes to this Agreement)
The Licensor may change this agreement. The changed agreement applies to versions of the Software distributed after the change. The latest agreement is published at the official distribution site (Article 13).

Article 12 (Governing Law and Jurisdiction)
This agreement is governed by the laws of Japan. For any dispute relating to this agreement, the district court having jurisdiction over the Licensor's location shall be the exclusive agreed court of first instance.

Article 13 (Official Distribution Site and Contact)
The official distribution site of the Software is below. Contact with the Licensor (requests for redistribution permission, inquiries and bug reports) is also accepted through Issues there.
https://github.com/yunatype/yunatype
